{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgAQVhFmsPLG4rS8v8b4m","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I loosened `responseWriter.Hijack` (`response_writer.go:111`). It used to refuse to hijack whenever `Written()` was true, which included the case where only the headers had gone out (`size == 0`). That broke websocket libraries that set the status header before they hijack the connection. Now it only returns `errHijackAlreadyWritten` once body bytes have actually been written (`size > 0`).\n\nI added a test case, \"hijack after header write should succeed\", to `TestResponseWriterHijackAfterWrite`. It fails without the fix and passes with it (GATE PASS).\n\n**Not checked:** I didn't run the full test suite or try a real websocket library. The test uses the existing mock hijacker. One thing to be aware of: once the headers are written, the underlying `net/http` hijack will still be refused if the response writer has already flushed them to the client."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1624,"cache_read_input_tokens":33911,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":1624,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":6,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"79247c4a-ee3f-4744-b780-2fcc158b2e2a","uuid":"7925c1b9-8eac-45f5-a5f1-4b72606589c1","timestamp":"2026-10-18T21:23:24.761Z","request_id":"req_011CgAQVh37uxADVEXLWCnv5"}
